    <description>PDFGeek does the PDF jobs the online tools charge for, entirely on your own machine.
Nothing is uploaded, there are no file-count caps and there is no hourly throttle.

* Merge any number of PDFs, in an order you set
* Split into one file per page, or into fixed-size chunks
* Extract or remove pages, with print-dialog-style ranges
* Rotate by 90, 180 or 270 degrees, whole document or selected pages
* Reorder a document by listing the pages you want
* Watermark every page, with control over size, opacity and angle
* Encrypt with AES-128, choosing whether printing and text-copying stay allowed
* Remove a password from a document you can already open

The only network call the application makes is the update check, and that only runs when you
press the button. Free at home and at work, with no Pro tier, no adverts and no bundled offers.

Open source under GPL-3.0. The .NET 8 runtime is bundled, so there is nothing to install first.</description>
    <summary>Free offline PDF toolkit for Windows - merge, split, extract, rotate, watermark, lock</summary>
